  "reason": "The source assertion explicitly states 'Dendrites contain ligand-gated ion channels'. The available relation 'contain' is defined as 'SOURCE possesses or includes TARGET as a constituent part', which matches the semantic meaning of the text exactly. Other relations like 'contained_in' reverse the direction (dendrites would be the target), and 'occur_in' changes the semantic nuance from possession/constituent part to mere presence/location. The qualifier 'upon neurotransmitter binding' describes the condition of the channels but does not alter the fundamental structural relationship being asserted."
